      <reaction compartment="compartment_7660" fast="false" id="reaction_110375" metaid="metaid_9" name="Excision of the abasic sugar phosphate (5'dRP) residue at the single strand break" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">After incision of the DNA strand 5' to the apurinic/apyrimidinic (AP) site by APEX1 (APE1), POLB (DNA polymerase beta) excises the 5'-terminal abasic deoxyribose phosphate (5'-dRP), thus removing the AP site (Bennet et al. 1997).</p>
        </notes>
